# Offline-restore artifacts (7b-3): the pre-restore safety snapshot (the whole
# member directory in plaintext — REAL PII in a PUBLIC repo), the restore report,
# the forensic audit entry and the Ghost discrepancy report. Unanchored, so it
# matches at any depth: the tool's default out-dir is relative to the working
# directory, and the documented invocation (`npm run restore --workspace apps/api`)
# runs with cwd `apps/api/`, so they land in `apps/api/restore-artifacts/`.
restore-artifacts/

# Prepared UAT photo fixtures (Stage 1.2, OFC-249): ~15 MB of WEBP derivatives
# produced by `prepare:uat-photos` and destined for the private UAT fixtures
# bucket. The faces are synthetic, so this is bulk rather than PII — but the same
# prefix holds the tester roster, and a corpus of binaries has no business in a
# source repo either way. Unanchored for the same reason as the line above: the
# tool's --out is relative to whatever directory it is invoked from.
uat-artifacts/
